fatiguing metal and plastic, but on a regular bike your legs do all the work and you get tired. On an e-bike, the motor provides assistance, so your muscles do less work and you finish fresher. The e-bike’s metal frame didn’t suddenly become immune to fatigue—it just started helping you. **In short:** The metal-and-plastic parts not tiring is a property of nearly all prostheses, not just bionic ones. The difference maker is the active, powered assistance that spares the user’s own muscles from burning out. That’s the physiological root of the reduced fatigue, not the inert material.
